---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const [latestPost] = (await getCollection('blog', ({ data }) => !data.draft))
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf() - a.data.pubDate.valueOf());
---
<BaseLayout
  title="CohenHolmes — Security, Identity & AI"
  description="CohenHolmes — Kaine Cohen's notes and tools on identity, security and AI governance across Microsoft 365. Conditional Access, AI governance, and email authentication."
  canonicalPath="/"
  ogDescription="Security, identity, and the practical realities of AI adoption."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" slot="head" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "CohenHolmes",
    "url": "https://cohenholmes.co.uk/",
    "sameAs": ["https://linkedin.com/in/kainecohen"],
    "founder": {
      "@type": "Person",
      "name": "Kaine Cohen",
      "jobTitle": "Security and AI Governance Consultant"
    },
    "knowsAbout": [
      "Microsoft 365 security",
      "Identity and access management",
      "Conditional Access",
      "Information protection and compliance",
      "AI adoption and governance"
    ]
  })} />

  <section class="hero" id="about">
    <p class="eyebrow">Security, identity, AI</p>
    <h1>I write about <em>security</em>, identity, and the strange, useful edges of <em>AI</em>.</h1>

    <p class="intro">
      I work across identity, security and compliance in Microsoft 365 — and increasingly,
      how organisations observe, govern and secure the AI agents now running inside it.
      This is where I think out loud about both.
    </p>

    <p class="note">
      Most of what's here started as something I had to work out properly myself: a
      policy with no clean explanation anywhere, a rollout that could have gone wrong, a
      check I wanted to run and couldn't. The write-ups and the tools are the result.
    </p>

    <p class="note">
      I hold Microsoft certifications in information protection and compliance (SC-400)
      and Microsoft 365 administration (MS-102) — the grounding underneath the identity,
      security and AI-governance work above. I'm also dyslexic: a lot of how I explain
      things comes from needing to make them make sense to myself first.
    </p>

    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="/blog">Read my writing</a>
      <a class="button" href="https://linkedin.com/in/kainecohen" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn ↗</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="focus">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>What I'm thinking about</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <div class="kicker">Identity</div>
        <p>Turning on MFA is the easy part. Getting Conditional Access right — without locking yourself out — is the actual work.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <div class="kicker">Security</div>
        <p>Most incidents aren't clever. They're a legacy protocol nobody turned off, or a service account with a password from 2019.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <div class="kicker">AI</div>
        <p>The interesting question isn't whether Copilot can draft the email. It's what happens to everything it read to do it.</p>
      </article>

      <a class="card" href="/ca-builder">
        <div class="kicker">Tooling</div>
        <p>An interactive Conditional Access Policy Builder — plain-English input, live Microsoft Graph-style JSON out.</p>
        <span class="trust">Free · nothing submitted</span>
        <span class="more">Open the builder →</span>
      </a>

      <a class="card" href="/ai-governance-check">
        <div class="kicker">AI Governance</div>
        <p>A private, browser-only readiness check across data, identity, governance, agents and human oversight.</p>
        <span class="trust">Free · nothing submitted</span>
        <span class="more">Check your readiness →</span>
      </a>

      <a class="card" href="/mail-auth">
        <div class="kicker">Email authentication</div>
        <p>Build correct SPF, DKIM and DMARC records and a staged path from monitoring to enforcement.</p>
        <span class="trust">Free · nothing submitted</span>
        <span class="more">Open the builder →</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="story">
      <strong>The tools are the same instinct, made clickable</strong> — the thing I wanted
      to exist while I was working it out.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="writing">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Writing</h2>
    </div>

    <p class="story">
      I write about identity, security, and where AI fits in — usually working something out
      in public rather than reporting back once it's tidy.
    </p>
    <p class="story">
      Longer writing lives at the blog, hosted here rather than anywhere else.
    </p>

    <div class="links">
      <a href="/blog">Read the blog →</a>
      {latestPost && (
        <a href={`/blog/${latestPost.data.slug ?? latestPost.id}/`}>
          Latest: {latestPost.data.title} →
        </a>
      )}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="contact">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Say hello</h2>
    </div>

    <p class="story">
      I'm on LinkedIn — happy to talk identity, security, compliance, or where AI fits
      into any of them.
    </p>

    <div class="links">
      <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/kainecohen" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn ↗</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero{ padding-top:8px; }
  .eyebrow{
    margin:0 0 18px;
    font-family:var(--font-body);
    font-weight:500;
    font-size:0.78rem;
    letter-spacing:0.12em;
    text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--accent-text);
  }
  h1{
    max-width:16ch;
  }
  h1 em{ font-style:italic; font-weight:500; color:var(--accent); }

  .intro{
    max-width:52ch;
    margin-top:24px;
    font-size:clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.4rem);
    color:#4A4A5A;
  }
  .note{
    max-width:60ch;
    margin-top:18px;
    font-size:1rem;
    color:#2C2C3A;
  }

  .actions{
    display:flex;
    flex-wrap:wrap;
    gap:12px;
    margin-top:28px;
  }
  .button{
    display:inline-flex;
    align-items:center;
    gap:8px;
    padding:11px 18px;
    text-decoration:none;
    border-radius:100px;
    font-size:0.95rem;
    font-weight:500;
    border:1px solid #E3DFD3;
    background:var(--cream);
    color:var(--navy);
    transition:transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease, background 0.2s ease;
  }
  .button:hover{ transform:translateY(-1px); border-color:var(--accent); background:#F1E2D6; }
  .button.primary{
    background:var(--navy);
    color:var(--cream);
    border-color:var(--navy);
  }
  .button.primary:hover{ background:var(--accent-text); border-color:var(--accent-text); color:#fff; }
  .button:focus-visible{ outline:2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset:2px; }

  .section{ margin-top:84px; }
  .section-head{
    display:flex;
    align-items:flex-end;
    justify-content:space-between;
    gap:16px;
    padding-bottom:14px;
    border-bottom:1px solid #E3DFD3;
    margin-bottom:28px;
  }
  .section-head h2{ margin:0; }

  .grid{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap:18px;
  }
  .card{
    background:#FCFAF6;
    border:1px solid #E3DFD3;
    border-radius:16px;
    padding:22px 20px;
    box-shadow:0 8px 18px rgba(15,30,51,0.06);
  }
  a.card{
    text-decoration:none;
    transition:transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;
  }
  a.card:hover{ transform:translateY(-2px); border-color:var(--accent); }
  a.card:focus-visible{ outline:2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset:2px; }
  .card .kicker{
    font-family:var(--font-body);
    color:var(--accent-text);
    font-weight:500;
    font-size:0.72rem;
    letter-spacing:0.11em;
    text-transform:uppercase;
    margin-bottom:10px;
  }
  .card p{ margin:0; color:#4A4A5A; font-size:0.95rem; }
  .card .trust{
    display:block;
    margin-top:10px;
    font-family:var(--font-mono);
    font-size:0.7rem;
    letter-spacing:0.03em;
    color:var(--muted);
  }
  .card .more{
    display:inline-block;
    margin-top:8px;
    font-size:0.85rem;
    color:var(--navy);
  }

  .story{
    max-width:68ch;
    margin-top:18px;
    font-size:1.02rem;
    color:#4A4A5A;
  }
  .story strong{ color:var(--navy); }

  .links{
    display:flex;
    flex-wrap:wrap;
    gap:10px;
    margin-top:18px;
  }
  .links a{
    text-decoration:none;
    color:var(--navy);
    border:1px solid #E3DFD3;
    border-radius:100px;
    padding:10px 14px;
    font-size:0.92rem;
    background:var(--cream);
    transition:border-color 0.2s ease;
  }
  .links a:hover{ border-color:var(--accent); }
</style>
